-- The definition half of a cross-IMPORT pair about contracts
-- (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118). ok/section-given-import-contract-call.l4 imports it.
--
-- `pay leg` reads the section GIVEN `dl`, which has a default of 5, so Alice
-- has until 5 to pay. `pay then deliver` reads two, `dl` and `rate`. `plain leg`
-- reads nothing. `unset leg` reads a section GIVEN with no default, so nothing
-- can say which branch it takes.
-- Discharge runs per module, so when THIS file is discharged `pay leg` and
-- `unset leg` each gain the section GIVEN they read as a trailing input. An
-- importer's call site is not rewritten, so an importer that names one of them
-- is naming a closure that must be applied to this module's own cell before it
-- is a contract.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
  deliver

§ `Terms`
    GIVEN dl IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`pay leg` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN dl
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

§§ `Rate`
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`pay then deliver` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN dl
    HENCE (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN rate
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "bob late")
    LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`plain leg` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

§ `Unset`
    GIVEN gate IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`unset leg` MEANS
    IF gate
    THEN PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
    ELSE FULFILLED
